// Round 8: `sword_drawn: true` added. A fresh level leaves the right hand empty on the original, so the press
// at tick 5 only drew the sword and the earlier capture never swung (the dummy kept 50 health); with the
// sword given and its draw run out first, the press attacks. The port starts with the sword in hand.
// Front assassination of an unaware guard (melee.md F4, ported): the assassinate move sets have Front / Left /
// Right / Back variants chosen by the side the player is on (0x00BBA970), m_fAllowedAngleFromTargetDir is 360, and
// the gate is the target's awareness (m_AssassinateOnAwareness: Unaware, Surprised, Suspicious, Begging), not the
// direction. The dummy is an idle guard with a brain and no faction (Unaware). UNMEASURED on the original.
(
    name: "combat/melee_assassinate_front",
    system: Combat,
    map: "Playground",
    description: "Swing at an unaware guard 120 uu ahead that faces the player.",
    setup: (
        player: Some((sword_drawn: true, position: (-5300, 0, 96), yaw: 180, pitch: 0)),
        npcs: [(id: Some("dummy"), position: Some((-5420, 0, 92)), yaw: 0, state: Some("Idle"), faction: Some("None"))],
        settle: 30,
    ),
    ticks: 180,
    input: [(tick: 5, action: Press(Primary))],
    checkpoints: [
        (name: "assassinated", expect: [(metric: Count("Sim:Death@dummy[cause=Assassination]"), value: 1, tol: 0, source: "any side (m_fAllowedAngleFromTargetDir 360, the Front move set) of an Unaware NPC (0x00C0D8F0); before the port: a normal hit", status: Unmeasured)]),
    ],
    record: [Pawn, Npc("dummy"), SimEvents],
    capture: Some("as melee_assassinate_back, from the front"),
)